      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: Video to Pose Guide (FAB)",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Video to Pose Guide (FAB)\n\nTurns a clip of one or more people into a pose-guide video: an OpenPose-style skeleton on black, with the size, frame rate and length of the clip. Use it as the control video of a pose-driven workflow.\n\nThe same graph as Video to Pose Guide (SAM 3D Body), with FAB in place of SAM 3D Body Predict. FAB is a distilled SAM 3D Body with its own person detector, so the SAM 3.1 tracks and RT-DETR boxes are gone. Its pose data goes to core's Face Expression, Smooth and Render nodes as before.\n\n**Load Video** → **Trim Video** → MoGe field of view → **FAB Body Pose** → **Render 3D Body Pose** → **Save Video** (`output/video/pose_guide_fab_...`).\n\n**Licence to accept first.** FAB reads the model config of SAM 3D Body. Accept the licence on [facebook/sam-3d-body-dinov3](https://huggingface.co/facebook/sam-3d-body-dinov3) with the account whose token is `HF_TOKEN` in `.env`. Until then the node stops with a message.\n\n**SMPL, by hand.** FAB fits SMPL to each person. Register at [smpl.is.tue.mpg.de](https://smpl.is.tue.mpg.de), download SMPL 1.1.0 for Python and copy the neutral, male and female `.pkl` files to `models/body_models/smpl/` as `SMPL_NEUTRAL.pkl`, `SMPL_MALE.pkl` and `SMPL_FEMALE.pkl`.\n\nFAB's weights are for non-commercial research only.\n\n## Settings worth knowing\n\n- **FAB Body Pose, model**: FAB-L, the accurate one. FAB-S is smaller and faster.\n- **FAB Body Pose, max_people**: 8. People keep their order from frame to frame by box overlap.\n- **Render 3D Body Pose, render_style**: `openpose_2d`, with hands drawn DWPose-style and no face dots. `face_style` adds face landmarks, `openpose_3d` shades the skeleton as a 3D model, `scail` draws SCAIL-style 3D capsules, `mesh` renders the body mesh.\n- **Render 3D Body Pose, background**: left unconnected, so the canvas is black. Connect `images` from **Get Video Components** to draw over the clip instead.\n- **Trim Video, duration**: 5 seconds. 0 processes the whole clip.\n\n## Input Asset\n\n- [woman_holding_water_glass.mp4](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/woman_holding_water_glass.mp4)\n\n## Model Links\n\n**detection**\n\n- [sam_3d_body_dinov3_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam-3d-body/resolve/main/detection/sam_3d_body_dinov3_bf16.safetensors) (2.64 GB), for the mesh faces and colours; not run\n\n**geometry_estimation**\n\n- [moge_2_vitl_normal_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MoGe/resolve/main/geometry_estimation/moge_2_vitl_normal_fp16.safetensors) (631.2 MB)\n\n**FAB** (the node downloads these on first use; profile `fab-pose-guide`)\n\n- [noahcao/FAB](https://huggingface.co/noahcao/FAB): `fab-l/model.pt` (1.7 GB) and `shared/` (0.2 GB), into `models/fab/weights/`\n- FAB's source, [noahcao/FAB](https://github.com/noahcao/FAB) at a pinned commit (Apache-2.0), into `models/fab/code/`\n- MHR's model and SMPL conversion files ([facebookresearch/MHR](https://github.com/facebookresearch/MHR), Apache-2.0), and SPIN's H36M joint regressor\n\n## Where this workflow comes from\n\nA copy of Video to Pose Guide (SAM 3D Body), itself derived from ComfyUI's `utility_sam3d_body` template (Comfy-Org/workflow_templates, MIT). Changed: SAM 3D Body Predict, SAM 3.1 tracking and RT-DETR replaced by FAB Body Pose, and the output prefix."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Video to Pose Guide (SAM 3D Body)\n\nTurns a clip of one or more people into a pose-guide video: an OpenPose-style skeleton on black, with the size, frame rate and length of the clip. Use it as the control video of a pose-driven workflow.\n\nThe skeleton is projected from a 3D body fit, not read from 2D keypoints, and the motion is smoothed over time before it is drawn.\n\n**Load Video** → **Trim Video** → detection (RT-DETR boxes, SAM 3.1 tracks, MoGe field of view) → **SAM 3D Body** → **Render 3D Body Pose** → **Save Video** (`output/video/pose_guide_...`).\n\n## Settings worth knowing\n\n- **Render 3D Body Pose, render_style**: `openpose_2d`, with hands drawn DWPose-style and no face dots. `face_style` adds face landmarks, `openpose_3d` shades the skeleton as a 3D model, `scail` draws SCAIL-style 3D capsules, `mesh` renders the body mesh.\n- **Render 3D Body Pose, background**: left unconnected, so the canvas is black. Connect `images` from **Get Video Components** to draw over the clip instead.\n- **Trim Video, duration**: 5 seconds. 0 processes the whole clip.\n\n## Input Asset\n\n- [woman_holding_water_glass.mp4](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Comfy-Org/workflow_templates/refs/heads/main/input/woman_holding_water_glass.mp4)\n\n## Model Links\n\n**checkpoints**\n\n- [sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam3.1/resolve/main/checkpoints/sam3.1_multiplex_fp16.safetensors) (1.63 GB)\n\n**detection**\n\n- [sam_3d_body_dinov3_bf16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/sam-3d-body/resolve/main/detection/sam_3d_body_dinov3_bf16.safetensors) (2.64 GB)\n\n**geometry_estimation**\n\n- [moge_2_vitl_normal_fp16.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MoGe/resolve/main/geometry_estimation/moge_2_vitl_normal_fp16.safetensors) (631.2 MB)\n\n**diffusion_models**\n\n- [rt_detr_v4-x-hgnet_fp32.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/SDPose/resolve/main/diffusion_models/rt_detr_v4-x-hgnet_fp32.safetensors) (236.3 MB)\n\n## Where this workflow comes from\n\nDerived from ComfyUI's `utility_sam3d_body` template (Comfy-Org/workflow_templates, MIT). Changed: the render style (body mesh over the clip, now a 2D skeleton on black) and the output prefix. The 3D animation export (**Create 3D Animation File** and the 3D save node) is removed here. It stays in ComfyUI's template, which the `sam3d-body-mocap` profile serves.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
  ],
